WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:17.648
The Lemonade Detectives looked at Hannah in surprise.

2
00:00:17.649 --> 00:00:22.067
"Mrs. Sweet is dating Mr. Moss?" Maggie said.

3
00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:27.924
Hannah giggled. "My mom works at a fancy restaurant on Baker Street.

4
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:33.950
She says Mr. Moss and Mrs. Sweet have been there a lot recently."

5
00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:38.417
Henry was surprised by Hannah's news. Was it a clue?

6
00:00:38.418 --> 00:00:41.374
By now it was late afternoon.

7
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:47.037
He looked over at the Dessert Den, and saw that the electrician's truck was still there.

8
00:00:47.038 --> 00:00:53.242
So they still couldn't talk to Mr. Tate.

9
00:00:53.243 --> 00:00:57.319
"Did you know that Mrs. Sweet and Mr. Moss were dating?"

10
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.499
Henry asked his friends as they wandered toward their bikes.

11
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.809
"Nope. Mr. Moss usually spreads around all the town gossip," Cole said with a smile.

12
00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:11.187
"I guess he doesn't like to gossip about himself though!"

13
00:01:11.188 --> 00:01:18.269
"Maybe Mr. Moss pushed over our bikes because he knew we were investigating his girlfriend," said Maggie.

14
00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:24.484
"Maybe," Henry said. "But Mr. Moss is just as nice as Mrs. Sweet.

15
00:01:24.485 --> 00:01:29.319
I can't believe he'd do something like that and then lie about it to us."

16
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.811
"Me neither." Cole gulped.

17
00:01:31.812 --> 00:01:35.577
"Not unless he knows Mrs. Sweet is guilty, that is."

18
00:01:35.578 --> 00:01:40.705
"I have an idea," Henry said. "Let's go talk to my dad."

19
00:01:40.706 --> 00:01:46.082
Maggie groaned. "You want to ride back to town again?" she said.

20
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:50.343
"Anyway, I thought you didn't want your dad to investigate Mrs. Sweet."

21
00:01:50.344 --> 00:01:55.102
"He's written a few stories about West Belltown," Henry reminded her.

22
00:01:55.103 --> 00:01:59.963
"He might know something useful."

23
00:01:59.964 --> 00:02:03.045
They rode to the newspaper office.

24
00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:08.026
Henry's dad was in the reception area shuffling through some papers.

25
00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:13.685
"Hello, kids!" he greeted them with a smile. "What brings you here?"

26
00:02:13.686 --> 00:02:17.308
"We're working on a tough case," Henry said.

27
00:02:17.309 --> 00:02:20.634
"We were hoping we could talk to you about it."

28
00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:23.982
"Sure." Henry's dad checked his watch.

29
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:32.796
"I have to go to a meeting in a few minutes. But we can talk until then."

30
00:02:32.797 --> 00:02:35.009
He led the way to his office.

31
00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:41.973
After he closed the door, Henry and his friends told him all about the mystery.

32
00:02:41.974 --> 00:02:47.986
"Wow," Henry's dad said when they finished. "That's quite a story."

33
00:02:47.987 --> 00:02:51.484
"You can't tell anyone, Uncle Kevin," Maggie said.

34
00:02:51.485 --> 00:02:54.941
"We don't want to ruin Mrs. Sweet's reputation."

35
00:02:54.942 --> 00:02:59.393
Henry's dad smiled. "I can keep a secret.

36
00:02:59.394 --> 00:03:04.974
But I'm sure the flavor theft is just some kind of misunderstanding."

37
00:03:04.975 --> 00:03:09.567
"I hope so," Henry said. "But how can we prove it?

38
00:03:09.568 --> 00:03:13.873
Do you have any information that could help us crack the case?"

39
00:03:13.874 --> 00:03:17.394
"I'm afraid not," his father said.

40
00:03:17.395 --> 00:03:21.402
"But it sounds like you still have a few clues to investigate.

41
00:03:21.403 --> 00:03:25.187
Like the timing of the two signs, for instance."

42
00:03:25.188 --> 00:03:27.509
"Yeah." Cole bit his lip.

43
00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.971
"But what if we find out Mr. Tate had the flavor on his sign first?

44
00:03:31.972 --> 00:03:34.519
That means Mrs. Sweet is the culprit."

45
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.155
Henry's dad shrugged.

46
00:03:37.156 --> 00:03:42.486
"Being a good detective, or a good reporter, means looking for the truth.

47
00:03:42.487 --> 00:03:48.081
You have to dig up all the facts, even if they lead to an answer you don't like."

48
00:03:48.082 --> 00:03:53.710
There was a knock on the door. "Time for the meeting, Kevin," a woman called.

49
00:03:53.711 --> 00:03:56.796
"Thanks." Henry's dad stood.

50
00:03:56.797 --> 00:04:01.981
"Sorry, kids. I have to go. We can talk more later if you like."

51
00:04:01.982 --> 00:04:05.153
"Okay. Thanks, Dad."

52
00:04:05.154 --> 00:04:08.943
As Henry and his friends left the building, someone stepped toward them.

53
00:04:08.944 --> 00:04:10.823
It was Robby.

54
00:04:10.824 --> 00:04:15.064
"Hi," Cole greeted him. "What are you doing here?"

55
00:04:15.065 --> 00:04:21.477
"Looking for you guys." Robby looked miserable. "I need to apologize."

56
00:04:21.478 --> 00:04:24.119
"What for?" asked Maggie.

57
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.081
"For knocking over your bikes earlier," Robby said.

58
00:04:28.082 --> 00:04:32.934
"That was you?" Cole exclaimed. "Why'd you do it?"

59
00:04:32.935 --> 00:04:36.824
"I knew you were working for Mr. Tate," Robby said.

60
00:04:36.825 --> 00:04:41.842
"I'm mad at him because he ruined my parents' plans for a community garden.

61
00:04:41.843 --> 00:04:46.207
That's why I followed you to the Sweet Shop and knocked over your bikes."

62
00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:55.402
He sighed. "But when I told my dad what I did, he made me promise to find you and apologize. So I'm sorry."

63
00:04:55.403 --> 00:05:01.342
"It's okay," Henry said. "Are your parents mad at Mr. Tate too?"

64
00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:07.177
"I thought they were, but Dad says he's glad our neighborhood is getting some new businesses."

65
00:05:07.178 --> 00:05:10.925
Robby shrugged. "Maybe I am too.

66
00:05:10.926 --> 00:05:14.622
It might be cool to have a dessert place a few blocks from home."

67
00:05:14.623 --> 00:05:17.593
Robby said good-bye and moved on.

68
00:05:17.594 --> 00:05:21.536
"I guess that solves one mystery," Cole said.

69
00:05:21.537 --> 00:05:27.333
"Yeah. But it doesn't help with identifying the flavor thief," Henry said.

70
00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:30.874
"Or with clearing Mrs. Sweet's name."

71
00:05:30.875 --> 00:05:33.686
"I know how to do that," Maggie said.

72
00:05:33.687 --> 00:05:36.969
"We need to talk to Mr. Tate about that sign!"

73
00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:42.685
This time it was Cole who groaned. "It's getting late," he said.

74
00:05:42.686 --> 00:05:45.758
"Plus, Nathan's still selling lemonade for us.

75
00:05:45.759 --> 00:05:49.516
Do we really have to ride to West Belltown again?"

76
00:05:49.517 --> 00:05:54.085
"Yes!" Maggie insisted. "Come on!"

77
00:05:54.086 --> 00:06:00.603
She hopped on her bike and rode down the street.

78
00:06:00.604 --> 00:06:03.458
But suddenly she stopped short.

79
00:06:03.459 --> 00:06:06.725
"What is it?" Henry asked as he caught up.

80
00:06:06.726 --> 00:06:11.912
"Look!" Maggie pointed to Mrs. Sweet's flavor board.

81
00:06:11.913 --> 00:06:16.507
"Bubble gum banana swirl is gone!"
